      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "To solve the problem \\( 4^4 \\cdot 5^4 \\), we can use the property of exponents that states \\( (a \\cdot b)^n = a^n \\cdot b^n \\).\n\nHere, \\( a = 4 \\), \\( b = 5 \\), and \\( n = 4 \\). Applying the property, we get:\n\\[\n4^4 \\cdot 5^4 = (4 \\cdot 5)^4\n\\]\n\nNext, we calculate \\( 4 \\cdot 5 \\):\n\\[\n4 \\cdot 5 = 20\n\\]\n\nSo, the expression becomes:\n\\[\n(4 \\cdot 5)^4 = 20^4\n\\]\n\nNow, we need to compute \\( 20^4 \\). We can break this down using the property of exponents \\((a^m)^n = a^{mn}\\):\n\\[\n20^4 = (20^2)^2\n\\]\n\nFirst, calculate \\( 20^2 \\):\n\\[\n20^2 = 400\n\\]\n\nThen, calculate \\( 400^2 \\):\n\\[\n400^2 = 400 \\cdot 400 = 160000\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{160000}\n\\]",
